---
version: 2.0.2
title: parse diagnostic: Pooka rules about declarations
file: ./test/parser_error_test.gleam
test_name: pooka_rule_errors_rendering_test
---
Source:
module zoo

pub class Animal {}

class Chimera is Lion, Goat {}

class Point {
  var x = 0.0
  be move() {}
}

interface Printable is Showable {
  print() -> String { "default" }
}

actor Worker is Process {}

fn add(a, b) { a + b }

---
error: module name does not match its file
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:1:8
  │
1 │ module zoo
  │        ─┬─
  │         ╰─ this declares module `zoo`
  ╰─

`src/main.pooka` must declare `module main`.

note: A module is named after its file, without `.pooka`.

error: visibility modifiers do not exist
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:3:1
  │
3 │ pub class Animal {}
  │ ─┬─
  │  ╰─ `pub` is not a Pooka keyword
  ╰─

Ordinary names are public, and a leading `_` makes a declaration private.

error: multiple inheritance is not supported
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:5:22
  │
5 │ class Chimera is Lion, Goat {}
  │                      ───┬──
  │                         ╰─ a class can only extend one class
  ╰─

`Chimera` already extends `Lion`.

help: Describe additional behaviour with interfaces, using `with`.

error: classes cannot contain mutable fields
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:8:3
  │
8 │   var x = 0.0
  │   ─┬─
  │    ╰─ `var` is not valid inside a class
  ╰─

Expected an immutable `let` field, but found `var`.

note: Mutable state belongs in actors.

error: behaviours belong to actors
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:9:3
  │
9 │   be move() {}
  │   ─┬
  │    ╰─ `be` is only valid inside an actor
  ╰─

A `be` behaviour is an asynchronous actor entry point.

help: Remove `be` to declare an ordinary method.

error: interfaces cannot inherit
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:12:21
   │
12 │ interface Printable is Showable {
   │                     ─┬
   │                      ╰─ `is` is not allowed on an interface
   ╰─

Interfaces do not inherit from other interfaces.

help: Let types implement several interfaces instead: `with A, B`.

error: interface methods cannot have bodies
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:13:21
   │
13 │   print() -> String { "default" }
   │                     ──────┬──────
   │                           ╰─ this body is not allowed
   ╰─

Interfaces contain method signatures only.

note: Shared behaviour belongs in ordinary functions or classes.

error: actors cannot inherit
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:16:14
   │
16 │ actor Worker is Process {}
   │              ─┬
   │               ╰─ `is` is not allowed on an actor
   ╰─

Actors do not participate in class inheritance.

help: Actors may implement interfaces with `with`.

error: named functions do not use `fn`
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:18:1
   │
18 │ fn add(a, b) { a + b }
   │ ─┬
   │  ╰─ `fn` is only for anonymous functions and function types
   ╰─

Named functions are written `name(parameters) { ... }`.

Found 9 errors.

